welcome back to the David Pakman show  I'm fair and cousins from Ring of Fire  sitting in for David Pakman today and  tomorrow obviously one of the biggest  stories even bigger than the indictments  recently handed out by the special  prosecutor's office is the tragedy that  took place in parkland Florida this past  week Donald Trump could not have botched  the response to this massacre any worse  than he actually did not only did the  man go down there and give a speech  where he didn't once mention the word  gun but he also posed for one of the  most idiotic photo shoots I think I have  ever seen any sitting president in my  lifetime perform sitting there with  first responders thumbs up big giant  smile on his face like he just won a  medal of honor 17 people most of them  children dead and Donald Trump sat there  smiling like an idiot as if he had done  anything to make it better anything to  help or as if this was some kind of  joyous occasion and then I mean I wish  that is as bad as his response got but  oh no it got so much worse  he then goes on Twitter decides to blame  Obama for this Democrats had the White  House and full control of both the House  and Senate for what two years and they  didn't do anything about gun control now  I hate to admit it I I have to agree  with him on that that's correct they did  nothing about it they should have but  they didn't they did during Obama's time  in office put in protections that made  it a little bit more harder for mentally  ill American citizens to buy weapons to  buy firearms which Donald Trump repealed  in his second month in office last year  but then after trying to pin this as an  Obama failure Obama screwed up Obama  Obama Obama every  bad that happens in the world in the  eyes of Donald Trump and Republicans so  he's going to go back to Obama so then  after that Donald Trump says yeah we got  a mental health issue problem in this  country we got to fix it that's that's  the real issue okay well again you  literally made it worse and you're not  taking any responsibility for that you  can whine and cry all day you all day  long that we have a mental health crisis  but at the end of the day you're the one  that repealed that rule that wasn't Paul  Ryan that wasn't Mitch McConnell that  wasn't the Koch brothers that was you  you signed your name on that Donald this  Massacre is 100% yours you own it you  helped this happen and when the next one  happens and it will it could be today it  could be tomorrow it could be by the end  of the week but it'll happen again  because they're not doing anything about  it again wish that was the end of it but  it's not Donald Trump after all of this  decides as he usually does he's gonna go  play golf Donald Trump spent part of his  time on Saturday morning golfing while  just a few miles away family members and  fellow students were lowering their  friends their children their brothers  their sisters into the ground as a  result of this massacre and Donald Trump  was out golfing and then later that  night Donald Trump finally decides to  talk to a few people about gun control  but it wasn't the victims families it  wasn't their friends it wasn't experts  it wasn't advocates it was the wealthy  members of mar-a-lago according to  stories to reports what's going on right  now  Saturday evening Donald Trump at  mar-a-lago in South Florida was asking  his wealthy donors wealthy buddies the  people who had to pay a $200,000 entry  Phee to get into mar-a-lago as members  he asked them what he should do about  gun control in the United States should  we do anything what how do we handle  this I don't know I'm not qualified to  hold this position as president of the  United States so why don't you tell me  mr. hedge fund manager mr. real estate  developer I'm sure you know more about  the issue than I do and I'm honestly  sure they probably do I'm sure that  pretty much anybody in this country  knows more about any issue better than  you mr. Trump and yeah people are angry  I'm angry you know a few weeks ago  there's a Thursday evening three weeks  ago I believe my wife who is a teacher  special education teacher mind you got a  call from her principal saying that a  student has made a threat against the  school that he was going to come in on  Friday and shoot students and teachers  anybody wearing blue that day was his  specific target they weren't close in  the school the threat had been made via  snapchat police were investigating there  will be an increased police presence at  the school on Friday at every entrance  every exit and patrolling the halls I  think they had about eight or nine  different police vehicles parked outside  all day long and that's what she went to  sleep to on that Thursday evening  knowing that she was going to work  tomorrow and a student had threatened to  come in and shoot everyone so Friday  morning she gets up terrified kisses the  kids goodbye a little bit longer than  usual game extra hug not knowing if she  was coming home that day I didn't know  if she'd come home that day she did know  event took place before school began  they found the kid he was arrested  crisis averted  that's not what happened in Parkland  that's not what happened at too many of  these schools or churches or nightclubs  or malls kids went to school that day it  didn't come home ever  and Trump was golfing while their bodies  were being put into the ground

